    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM Microorganism Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "A genus of enveloped, pleomorphically spherical viruses in the family Paramyxoviridae. The genome is composed of a linear single-strand of negative sense RNA. The Henipavirus natural reservoir is considered to be fruit bats of the Pteropodidae family and cause influenza-like illness in humans." ;
    flat:parents "C14307" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Virus" ;
    flat:synonyms "Henipavirus|HENIPAVIRUS" ;
.

