    flat:definition "A genus of enveloped, spherical or pleomorphic viruses with a capsid with T=16 icosahedral symmetry and surrounded by amorphous tegument, in the family Herpesviridae. The genome is composed of monopartite, linear double-stranded DNA. Varicelloviruses are found in mammals and cause chickenpox and shingles in humans." ;
    flat:parents "C14217" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Virus" ;
    flat:synonyms "Varicellovirus|VARICELLOVIRUS|Varicellavirus" ;
.

