    flat:code "C117997" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C117997>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC Clinical Classification Category Terminology|CDISC Clinical Classification Terminology|CDISC QRS Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "A standardized rating scale originally developed by Chouinard et al in 1980, which is used to measure drug-induced extrapyramidal symptoms (EPS) or 4 types of drug-induced movement disorders (DIMD): parkinsonism, akathisia, dystonia, and tardive dyskinesia. The questionnaire contains 28 questions and generates 4 subscales and 4 clinical global impression severity (CGI-S) scales." ;
    flat:parents "C118969" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Intellectual Product" ;
    flat:synonyms "Extrapyramidal Symptom Rating Scale-Abbreviated Clinical Classification|ESRS-A|ESRSA|ESRSA1" ;
.

