    flat:definition "A species of motile, unicellular eukaryotic amoebae within the family of Acanthamoebidae. A. palestinensis is placed in morphological group III with a 18s rRNA gene sequence type of T2. Members of this group are characterized by the presence of thin, smooth ectocysts and round endocysts. This species is a human pathogen and may cause granulomatous amoebic encephalitis and amoebic keratitis." ;
    flat:parents "C118934" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Eukaryote" ;
    flat:synonyms "Acanthamoeba palestinensis|ACANTHAMOEBA PALESTINENSIS" ;
