    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM Microorganism Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "A species of tapeworm in the family Hymenolepididae. The lifecycle of H. nana involves insects as the intermediate host and rodents or humans as the definitive host. Eggs may also be transferred directly from person to person." ;
