    flat:definition "A standardized rating scale developed by the Haemo-QoL Study Group in 2002, which is used to measure the physical and emotional impacts on quality of life in children and adolescents with hemophilia. The children's long version age group II questionnaire contains 64 items for children 8 to 12 years of age." ;
