    flat:definition "A subgroup of Legionella pneumophila differentiated by its antigenicity. Serogroup 1 is the serogroup most commonly associated with disease, responsible for 70-90% of cases of legionellosis." ;
    flat:parents "C86489" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Bacterium" ;
    flat:synonyms "Legionella pneumophila Serogroup 1|LEGIONELLA PNEUMOPHILA SEROGROUP 1" ;
.

