    flat:definition "An organ that is part of the hematopoietic and immune systems. It is composed of the white pulp and the red pulp and is surrounded by a capsule. It is located in the left hypochondriac region. Its functions include lymphocyte production, blood cell storage, and blood cell destruction." ;
    flat:display%20name "Spleen" ;
    flat:parents "C13018" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Body Part, Organ, or Organ Component" ;
    flat:synonyms "Spleen|Reticuloendothelial System, Spleen|SPLEEN|Splenic|Splenic structure (body structure)|spleen|spleen|splenic" ;
.

