    flat:definition "The correction on the aggregate of QT intervals using individual probabilistic QT/RR slopes for each subject based on the measurement of QT intervals from multiple beats within a single ECG or from a defined time period within a continuous ECG. The method of aggregation, which can vary, is typically a measure of central tendency, such as mean." ;
    flat:parents "C62085" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Quantitative Concept" ;
    flat:synonyms "Aggregate QTca Interval|QTCAAG|QTCAAG|QTca Interval, Aggregate|QTca Interval, Aggregate|QTca Interval, Aggregate" ;
.

