    flat:definition "A species of filamentous fungi in the phylum Zygomycota characterized by sporangiophores that arise from nodes at the point where the rhizoids are formed. R. oryzae is a causative agent of mucormycosis in immunocompromised individuals. This species is used in the fermentation of tempeh." ;
    flat:parents "C77196" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Fungus" ;
