    flat:definition "A technique for measuring anatomical densities in which a single X-ray beam, whose low and high energy is separated, is aimed at the bone or tissue of interest and x-ray absorption is assessed. This technique has multiple applications including the measurement of bone mineral density and bone mineral content and more novel applications such as breast density." ;
    flat:parents "C38101" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Diagnostic Procedure" ;
    flat:synonyms "Single Energy X-Ray Absorptiometry|SXA|SXA SCAN" ;
.

