    flat:synonyms "Histological Procedure|Histologic Procedure|Histological Technique|Histological Techniques|histologic examination" ;
.

ncit:C16681
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C16681" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C16681>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CRF7 Pathology Review Table|EWS Histology Table|EWS Variable Terminology|GCT Histology Table|GCT Variable Terminology|GDC Terminology|GDC Value Terminology|HL Histology Table|HL Variable Terminology|OS Histology Table|OS Variable Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "The study of the structure of the cells and their arrangement to constitute tissues and, finally, the association among these to form organs.  In pathology, the microscopic process of identifying normal and abnormal morphologic characteristics in tissues, by employing various cytochemical and immunocytochemical stains." ;
    flat:parents "C16344" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Biomedical Occupation or Discipline" ;
    flat:synonyms "Histology|HISTOLOGY|HISTOLOGY|HISTOLOGY|HISTOLOGY|Microanatomy|histology" ;
.

ncit:C16683
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C16683" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C16683>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM Binding Agent for Immunogenicity Tests Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology|CTRP Biomarker Terminology|CTRP Molecular Genetic Biomarker Terminology|CTRP Terminology|GDC Terminology|GDC Value Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "Linker Histone H1 interacts with DNA between nucleosome units in mediating chromatin compaction into higher order structures. Histones are basic nuclear proteins responsible for the nucleosome structure of eukaryotic chromatin. Repeating nucleosome units contain two molecules each of core Histones H2A, H2B, H3, and H4 that form an octamer complex around which approximately 146 base pairs of DNA is wrapped. (NCI)" ;
    flat:display%20name "Histone H1" ;
    flat:parents "C16687" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Amino Acid, Peptide, or Protein" ;
    flat:synonyms "Histone H1|H1|HISTONE H1" ;
.

ncit:C16684
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C16684" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C16684>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM Binding Agent for Immunogenicity Tests Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology|CTRP Biomarker Terminology|CTRP Molecular Genetic Biomarker Terminology|CTRP Terminology|GDC Terminology|GDC Value Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "Slightly lysine rich histone.  One of four histones assembled into a nucleosomal core octamer.  Various posttranslationally modified forms and variants exist.  Combines with histone H2B in a heterodimer; two H2A/H2B dimers are incorporated in the nucleosomal octamer." ;
    flat:display%20name "Histone H2A" ;
    flat:parents "C114866" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Amino Acid, Peptide, or Protein" ;
    flat:synonyms "Histone H2A|H2A|H2A|HIST1H2A|HISTONE H2A|Histone 2A" ;
.

ncit:C16685
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C16685" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C16685>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM Binding Agent for Immunogenicity Tests Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology|CTRP Biomarker Terminology|CTRP Molecular Genetic Biomarker Terminology|CTRP Terminology|GDC Terminology|GDC Value Terminology|Pediatric Oncology Target Genes/Proteins Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "Histone H3 is a core subunit of the eukaryotic nucleosome complex. Histones are basic nuclear proteins responsible for the nucleosome structure of chromatin. Repeating nucleosome units contain two molecules each of Histones H2A, H2B, H3, and H4 that form an octamer complex around which approximately 146 base pairs of DNA is wrapped. Linker Histone H1 interacts with DNA between nucleosome units in mediating chromatin compaction into higher order structures. (NCI)" ;
    flat:display%20name "Histone H3" ;
    flat:parents "C16687" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Amino Acid, Peptide, or Protein" ;
    flat:synonyms "Histone H3|H3|HISTONE H3" ;
.

ncit:C16686
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C16686" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C16686>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM Binding Agent for Immunogenicity Tests Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology|CTRP Biomarker Terminology|CTRP Molecular Genetic Biomarker Terminology|CTRP Terminology|GDC Terminology|GDC Value Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "Histone H4 (103 aa, ~11 kDa) is encoded by the human H4C1, H4C2, H4C3, H4C4, H4C5, H4C6, H4C6, H4C8, H4C9, H4C11, H4C12, H4C13, H4C14, H4C15, H4-16 genes. This protein plays a role in nucleating the formation of high order chromatin structures as a part of nucleosomes." ;
    flat:display%20name "Histone H4" ;
    flat:parents "C16687" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Amino Acid, Peptide, or Protein" ;
    flat:synonyms "Histone H4|H4|HIST1H4|HISTONE H4|Histone 1, H4" ;
.

ncit:C16687
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C16687" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C16687>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM Binding Agent for Immunogenicity Tests Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology|CTRP Biomarker Terminology|CTRP Molecular Genetic Biomarker Terminology|CTRP Terminology|GDC Property Terminology|GDC Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "Major protein component of chromatin.  Highly conserved basic proteins, originally classified into classes based on the relative amounts of arginine and lysine in each protein.  The various classes are now termed H1, H2A, H2B, H3, and H4.  In chromatin, they are found in an octamer, containing two each of H2A, H2B, H3, and H4, complexed with DNA in nucleosomes.  The histones in the octamer complex are also known as the core histones.  The H1 class of histones, termed the linker histones, is loosely associated with the nucleosome." ;
    flat:display%20name "Histone" ;
    flat:parents "C18073" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Amino Acid, Peptide, or Protein" ;
    flat:synonyms "Histone|HISTONE|histone|histone family|histone_family" ;
.

ncit:C16689
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C16689" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C16689>" ;
    flat:definition "A protein produced by the human immunodeficiency virus that functions as a viral anti-receptor attachment protein. The protein is localized to the viral envelope and mediates fusion between viral and cellular membranes." ;
    flat:parents "C16610" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Amino Acid, Peptide, or Protein" ;
    flat:synonyms "HIV Envelope Protein gp120|gp120 ENV Glycoprotein" ;
.

ncit:C16690
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C16690" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C16690>" ;
    flat:definition "A protein produced by the human immunodeficiency virus that functions as a viral attachment protein on the viral envelope. This transmembrane protein is a glycoprotein that non-covalently anchors gp120 to the virus particle." ;
    flat:parents "C16610" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Amino Acid, Peptide, or Protein|Biologically Active Substance" ;
    flat:synonyms "HIV Envelope Protein gp41" ;
.

ncit:C16691
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C16691" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C16691>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM Binding Agent for Immunogenicity Tests Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology|CTRP Biomarker Terminology|CTRP Molecular Genetic Biomarker Terminology|CTRP Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "HLA class I histocompatibility antigen, A-2 alpha chain (365 aa, ~41 kDa) is encoded by the human HLA-A gene. This protein is involved in antigen presentation." ;
    flat:display%20name "HLA Class I Histocompatibility Antigen, A-2 Alpha Chain" ;
    flat:parents "C113513" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Amino Acid, Peptide, or Protein|Immunologic Factor" ;
    flat:synonyms "HLA Class I Histocompatibility Antigen, A-2 Alpha Chain|HLA Class I Histocompatibility Antigen, A*02 Alpha Chain|HLA-A|HLA-A Class I Antigen 2|HLA-A Histocompatibility Type Antigen 2|HLA-A Histocompatibility Type Antigen*02|HLA-A*02|HLA-A2|HLA-A2|HLA-A2 ANTIGEN|HLA-A2 Antigen|MHC Class I Antigen A*02|MHC Class I Antigen A*2|Major Histocompatibility Complex, Class I, A2 Antigen" ;
.

ncit:C16692
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C16692" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C16692>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CTRP Biomarker Terminology|CTRP Molecular Genetic Biomarker Terminology|CTRP Terminology|GDC Terminology|GDC Value Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "Encoded by multiple HLA-DRA and HLA-DRB genes in a complex variable 5 cM region of MHC between HLA-B and -D, HLA-DR Antigens are Class II histocompatibility transmembrane glycoprotein heterodimers of alpha (heavy, 35-kD) and beta (light, 27-kD) chains. Located predominantly on B cells and macrophages, HLA-DR antigens function in antigen presentation to regulatory T cells in the immune response and in self/nonself discrimination. Invariant alpha and polymorphic beta chains have glycosylated N-termini, hydrophobic membrane regions, and hydrophilic C-termini. The heterodimer consists of 4 extracellular domains; invariant alpha-1, polymorphic N-terminal beta-1, and conserved Ig-like alpha-2 and beta-2. Alpha-1 and alpha-2 contain disulfide loops. Beta-1 contains 2 small variable regions. Alpha sequences have relatively simple structure; beta chains carry the major polymorphic determinants." ;
    flat:display%20name "HLA-DR Antigen" ;
    flat:parents "C20705" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Amino Acid, Peptide, or Protein|Immunologic Factor" ;
    flat:synonyms "HLA-DR Antigen|HLA-DR|HLA-DR|HLA-DR|Human Leukocyte Antigen - DR Isotype|Human Leukocyte Antigen-DR Isotype" ;
.

