    flat:definition "The class of all enzymes catalyzing oxidoreduction reactions (EC class 1). The substrate that is oxidized is regarded as a hydrogen donor. The systematic name is based on donor: acceptor oxidoreductase. The recommended name will be dehydrogenase, wherever this is possible; as an alternative, reductase can be used. Oxidase is only used in cases where O2 is the acceptor. (Enzyme Nomenclature, 1992, p9)" ;
    flat:parents "C16554" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Amino Acid, Peptide, or Protein|Enzyme" ;
    flat:synonyms "Oxidoreductase|EC 1" ;
.

