    flat:definition "Kinases that phosphorylate protein tyrosine residues. These kinases play major roles in mitogenic signalling, and can be divided into two subfamilies: receptor tyrosine kinases, that have an extracellular ligand-binding domain, a single transmembrane domain, and an intracellular tyrosine kinase domain; and nonreceptor tyrosine kinases, which are soluble, cytoplasmic kinases. (Dictionary of Cell and Molecular Biology Online)" ;
    flat:parents "C17018" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Amino Acid, Peptide, or Protein|Enzyme" ;
    flat:synonyms "Protein Tyrosine Kinase|EC 2.7.10|PTK|Protein-Tyrosine Kinase|Tyrosine Kinase|Tyrosine Protein Kinase|Tyrosine-Protein Kinase|Tyrosine-Specific Protein Kinase" ;
.

