    flat:definition "An assay that is used to detect the presence of a toxin in a biological sample by inoculating two sets of tissue cell cultures, one prepared with anti-toxin and one prepared without anti-toxin, with filtrates of the sample and assessing for a cytopathic effect after an incubation period." ;
    flat:parents "C150876" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Laboratory Procedure" ;
    flat:synonyms "Cell Cytotoxicity Neutralization Assay|CCNA|CCNA|CELL CYTOTOXICITY NEUTRALIZATION ASSAY" ;
.

