    flat:definition "A standardized eight-item short version of the Medical Outcomes Study 36-Item Short-Form Health Survey (SF-36) that utilizes a five-point rating scale and a four week recall to assess health-related quality of life. The measured dimensions include general health, physical functioning, role-physical, bodily pain, vitality, social functioning, mental health, and role-emotional." ;
