    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM Microorganism Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "A betacoronavirus, first isolated in 2005, that utilizes 9-O-acetylated sialic acid as a receptor determinant and has hemagglutinin-esterase activity. It is associated with human respiratory infections, particularly the common cold, and febrile seizures." ;
    flat:parents "C113207" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Virus" ;
    flat:synonyms "Human Coronavirus HKU1|HCoV-HKU1|HUMAN CORONAVIRUS HKU1" ;
.

