    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM Binding Agent for Immunogenicity Tests Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "A group of autoimmune substances found in the neurons that may be comprised of (but not limited to) Hu, Tr, Yo and Ri proteins. They can be considered as neuronal autoantigens and are commonly associated with autoimmune neurodegenerative disorders related to cancer, such as paraneoplastic neurologic syndrome." ;
    flat:parents "C181353" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Immunologic Factor|Organic Chemical" ;
    flat:synonyms "Neuronal Nuclear Autoantigens|NEURONAL NUCLEAR AUTOANTIGENS" ;
.

