    flat:definition "Glutamate receptor 1 (906 aa, ~102 kDa) is encoded by the human GRIA1 gene. This protein is involved in L-glutamate- and glutamatergic agonist-dependent transport of sodium and calcium cations." ;
    flat:parents "C28505|C18106" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Amino Acid, Peptide, or Protein|Receptor" ;
