    flat:definition "The self-report version of a standardized questionnaire developed by the World Health Organization (WHO) in 2001 as a modification to the original Alcohol Use Disorder Identification Test (AUDIT). It contains three questions and utilizes a five-point response scale to screen for hazardous drinking." ;
    flat:parents "C91105" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Intellectual Product" ;
    flat:synonyms "Alcohol Use Disorders Identification Test-Concise Self-Report Version Questionnaire|ADTC02|AUDIT-C Self-Report Version|MODIFIED AUDIT-C FROM WHO AUDIT: SELF-REPORT VERSION 2001" ;
.

ncit:C225103
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C225103" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C225103>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC QRS Terminology|CDISC Questionnaire Category Terminology|CDISC Questionnaire Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "A standardized 16-item rating scale for symptoms of breast cancer that is comprised of disease-related, treatment side effects, and general function and well-being subscales. Originally developed by Cella et al. in 2011, it is a modified version of the 8-item Functional Assessment of Cancer Therapy - Breast Cancer Symptom Index (FBSI), incorporating additional items from the Functional Assessment of Chronic Illness Therapy (FACIT) measurement system." ;
    flat:parents "C91105" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Intellectual Product" ;
    flat:synonyms "National Comprehensive Cancer Network/Functional Assessment of Cancer Therapy-Breast Cancer Symptom Index-16 Version 2 Questionnaire|FAC032|NFBSI-16 V2|NFBSI-16 Version 2" ;
.

