    flat:definition "The outermost of the two pleural membranes. It consists of a thin basal layer of fibrous tissue upon which sits a continuous layer of mesothelial cells. The cells function to secrete the lubricant lining the pleural cavity." ;
    flat:parents "C12469" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Tissue" ;
    flat:synonyms "Parietal Pleura|PARIETAL PLEURA" ;
.

