    flat:definition "Any chemical, biological or physical agents that increase the risk of neoplasms in humans or animals.  Carcinogens include natural or synthesized compounds, certain viruses, and various sources of radiation.  A carcinogen may directly alter the genetic material of cells (genotoxic), thereby initiating or promoting the process of malignant transformation; it also may induce cancers by mechanisms that do not involve a direct alteration of cellular genetic material (non-genotoxic). (NCI04)" ;
