    flat:definition "Administration of a substance within the tissues surrounding a joint." ;
    flat:parents "C38291" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Functional Concept" ;
    flat:synonyms "Periarticular Route of Administration|P-ARTIC|P-ARTIC|PERIARTICULAR|PERIARTICULAR|PERIARTICULAR|Periarticular|Periarticular|Periarticular use" ;
.

ncit:C38293
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C38293" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C38293>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM Route of Administration Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology|EDQM Health Care Terminology|EDQM-HC Routes and Methods of Administration Terminology|FDA Structured Product Labeling Terminology|SPL Drug Route of Administration Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "Administration of a substance within the tissues surrounding a nerve or nerves." ;
    flat:parents "C38291" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Functional Concept" ;
    flat:synonyms "Perineural Route of Administration|P-NEURAL|P-NEURAL|PERINEURAL|PERINEURAL|PERINEURAL|Perineural|Perineural|Perineural use" ;
.

ncit:C38294
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C38294" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C38294>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM Route of Administration Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology|EDQM Health Care Terminology|EDQM-HC Routes and Methods of Administration Terminology|FDA Structured Product Labeling Terminology|SPL Drug Route of Administration Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "Administration of a substance within the tissues surrounding a tooth or teeth." ;
    flat:parents "C38197" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Functional Concept" ;
    flat:synonyms "Periodontal Route of Administration|P-ODONT|P-ODONT|PERIODONTAL|PERIODONTAL|PERIODONTAL|Periodontal|Periodontal|Periodontal use" ;
.

ncit:C38295
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C38295" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C38295>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM Route of Administration Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology|EDQM Health Care Terminology|EDQM-HC Routes and Methods of Administration Terminology|FDA Structured Product Labeling Terminology|SPL Drug Route of Administration Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "The introduction of a substance into the gastrointestinal tract by the way of the rectum, usually for systemic action. Depending on the molecular structure, drugs cross the rectal wall via either intercellular or tight junctions interconnecting the mucosal cells. Drug absorption is usually around 50% of normal oral dose. Due to the drainage pattern of the rectal veins, the hepatic first-pass effect tends to increase as the dosage form is placed deeper into the rectum. Solid suppositories represent greater than 98% of all rectal dosage forms." ;
    flat:parents "C38114" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Functional Concept" ;
    flat:synonyms "Rectal Route of Administration|Per Rectum|RECTAL|RECTAL|RECTAL|RECTAL|Rectal|Rectal|Rectal use" ;
.

ncit:C38296
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C38296" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C38296>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM Route of Administration Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology|EDQM Health Care Terminology|EDQM-HC Routes and Methods of Administration Terminology|FDA Structured Product Labeling Terminology|SPL Drug Route of Administration Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "The introduction of a substance behind the pons or behind the eyeball." ;
    flat:parents "C38114" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Functional Concept" ;
    flat:synonyms "Retrobulbar Route of Administration|RETRO|RETRO|RETROBULBAR|RETROBULBAR|RETROBULBAR|Retrobulbar|Retrobulbar|Retrobulbar use" ;
.

ncit:C38297
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C38297" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C38297>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM Route of Administration Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology|FDA Structured Product Labeling Terminology|SPL Drug Route of Administration Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "The introduction of a substance beneath the arachnoidal membrane" ;
    flat:parents "C38291" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Functional Concept" ;
    flat:synonyms "Subarachnoid Route of Administration|S-ARACH|S-ARACH|SUBARACHNOID|SUBARACHNOID|SUBARACHNOID|Subarachnoid" ;
.

ncit:C38298
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C38298" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C38298>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM Route of Administration Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology|EDQM Health Care Terminology|EDQM-HC Routes and Methods of Administration Terminology|FDA Structured Product Labeling Terminology|SPL Drug Route of Administration Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "The introduction of a substance beneath the conjunctiva." ;
    flat:parents "C38114" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Functional Concept" ;
    flat:synonyms "Subconjunctival Route of Administration|S-CONJUNC|S-CONJUNC|SUBCONJUNCTIVAL|SUBCONJUNCTIVAL|SUBCONJUNCTIVAL|Subconjunctival|Subconjunctival|Subconjunctival use" ;
.

ncit:C38299
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C38299" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C38299>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM Route of Administration Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology|EDQM Health Care Terminology|EDQM-HC Routes and Methods of Administration Terminology|FDA Structured Product Labeling Terminology|GDC Terminology|GDC Value Terminology|NICHD Terminology|SPL Drug Route of Administration Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "Drug administration beneath the skin. It provides for relatively slow, sustained release of the drug. The rate of absorption into the blood is perfusion-limited, proportional to the amount of drug at the site and can be enhanced by chemical or physical stimulation of blood flow. Subcutaneous administration minimizes the risks associated with intravascular injection: for subcutaneous infusions, external and implantable pumps are used." ;
    flat:parents "C38291" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Functional Concept" ;
    flat:synonyms "Subcutaneous Route of Administration|SC|SC|SC|SUBCUTANEOUS|SUBCUTANEOUS|SUBCUTANEOUS|Subcutaneous|Subcutaneous|Subcutaneous|Subcutaneous use|Subdermal Route of Administration" ;
.

ncit:C38300
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C38300" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C38300>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM Route of Administration Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology|EDQM Health Care Terminology|EDQM-HC Routes and Methods of Administration Terminology|FDA Structured Product Labeling Terminology|SPL Drug Route of Administration Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "Administration of a drug beneath the tongue. The route provides rapid absorption, the drug immediately enters the bloodstream without first passing through the intestinal wall and liver. However, most drugs cannot be taken this way because they may be absorbed incompletely or erratically." ;
    flat:parents "C38288" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Functional Concept" ;
    flat:synonyms "Sublingual Route of Administration|SL|SL|SUBLINGUAL|SUBLINGUAL|SUBLINGUAL|Sublingual|Sublingual|Sublingual use" ;
.

ncit:C38301
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C38301" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C38301>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM Route of Administration Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology|EDQM Health Care Terminology|EDQM-HC Routes and Methods of Administration Terminology|FDA Structured Product Labeling Terminology|SPL Drug Route of Administration Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "Administration of a drug beneath the mucous membrane." ;
    flat:parents "C38291" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Functional Concept" ;
    flat:synonyms "Submucosal Route of Administration|S-MUCOS|S-MUCOS|SUBMUCOSAL|SUBMUCOSAL|SUBMUCOSAL|Submucosal|Submucosal|Submucosal use" ;
.

ncit:C38304
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C38304" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C38304>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM Route of Administration Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology|EDQM Health Care Terminology|EDQM-HC Routes and Methods of Administration Terminology|FDA Structured Product Labeling Terminology|SPL Drug Route of Administration Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "The application of a drug to a certain area of the skin or mucous membrane (including the intra-organ application), or other tissue locally, so that the agent will take effect on the surface and/or on the underlying tissues." ;
    flat:parents "C38114" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Functional Concept" ;
    flat:synonyms "Topical Route of Administration|T|TOP|TOPIC|TOPICAL|TOPICAL|TOPICAL|TOPICAL|Topical|Topical|Topical" ;
.

ncit:C38305
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C38305" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C38305>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM Route of Administration Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology|EDQM Health Care Terminology|EDQM-HC Routes and Methods of Administration Terminology|FDA Structured Product Labeling Terminology|SPL Drug Route of Administration Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "Administration of a substance through the dermal layer of the skin into the systemic circulation by diffusion." ;
    flat:parents "C38114" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Functional Concept" ;
    flat:synonyms "Transdermal Route of Administration|Cutaneous Route of Administration|Percutaneous Route of Administration|T-DERMAL|T-DERMAL|TRANSDERMAL|TRANSDERMAL|TRANSDERMAL|Transdermal|Transdermal|Transdermal use" ;
.

ncit:C38307
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C38307" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C38307>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM Route of Administration Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology|EDQM Health Care Terminology|EDQM-HC Routes and Methods of Administration Terminology|FDA Structured Product Labeling Terminology|SPL Drug Route of Administration Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "Administration of a drug to an embryo in utero via systemic administration of the substance to the pregnant mother. Drugs cross the placenta through passive diffusion, active transport, pinocytosis and filtration. The properties of drugs that determine placental transfer by passive diffusion include molecular weight, pKa, lipid solubility and protein binding. Drugs with molecular weight of over 500 D are transferred incompletely. Drug metabolism and uptake can be altered by placental enzymes." ;
    flat:parents "C38114" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Functional Concept" ;
    flat:synonyms "Transplacental Route of Administration|T-PLACENT|T-PLACENT|TRANSPLACENTAL|TRANSPLACENTAL|TRANSPLACENTAL|Transplacental|Transplacental|Transplacental" ;
.

ncit:C38308
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C38308" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C38308>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM Route of Administration Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology|FDA Structured Product Labeling Terminology|SPL Drug Route of Administration Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "Administration of a drug through the wall of the trachea." ;
    flat:parents "C38114" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Functional Concept" ;
    flat:synonyms "Transtracheal Route of Administration|T-TRACHE|T-TRACHE|TRANSTRACHEAL|TRANSTRACHEAL|TRANSTRACHEAL|Transtracheal" ;
.

ncit:C38309
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C38309" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C38309>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM Route of Administration Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology|FDA Structured Product Labeling Terminology|SPL Drug Route of Administration Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "Administration of a drug across or through the tympanic cavity. This method reduces the total dose of medication, and allows high concentrations of drug to be delivered directly to the target tissue, while reducing systemic effects. Transtympanic medication can be administered through a needle puncture of the eardrum. If multiple injections are required, a myringotomy tube can be inserted." ;
    flat:parents "C38114" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Functional Concept" ;
    flat:synonyms "Transtympanic Route of Administration|T-TYMPAN|T-TYMPAN|TRANSTYMPANIC|TRANSTYMPANIC|TRANSTYMPANIC|Transtympanic" ;
.

ncit:C38310
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C38310" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C38310>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM Route of Administration Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology|FDA Structured Product Labeling Terminology|SPL Drug Route of Administration Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "Route of administration has not yet been assigned." ;
    flat:parents "C38114" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Functional Concept" ;
    flat:synonyms "Unassigned Route of Administration|UNAS|UNAS|UNASSIGNED|UNASSIGNED|UNASSIGNED" ;
.

ncit:C38311
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C38311" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C38311>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM Route of Administration Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology|FDA Structured Product Labeling Terminology|SPL Drug Route of Administration Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "The route of drug administration is unknown." ;
    flat:parents "C38114" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Functional Concept" ;
    flat:synonyms "Unknown Route of Administration|UNKNOWN|UNKNOWN|UNKNOWN|UNKNOWN|Unknown" ;
.

