ncit:C4872
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C4872" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C4872>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDRH Health Effects - Clinical Signs and Symptoms or Conditions Terminology|Cellosaurus Disease Terminology|Clinical Trials Search-Application Programming Interface Disease Category Terminology|CPTAC Codelists Terminology|CPTAC Medical Conditions Codelist|CPTAC Neoplasms Codelist|CPTAC Terminology|CTRP Disease Terminology|CTRP Terminology|CTS-API Disease Main Type Terminology|GDC Terminology|GDC Value Terminology|HemOnc Conditions|NCI CTEP SDC Breast Neoplasm, Miscellaneous Sub-Category Terminology|NCI CTEP Simplified Disease Classification Terminology|NCIt Neoplasm Core Terminology|NICHD Terminology|Pediatric Adverse Events Terminology Mapped to MedDRA|Pediatric Adverse Events Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "A carcinoma arising from the breast, most commonly the terminal ductal-lobular unit. It is the most common malignant tumor in females. Risk factors include country of birth, family history, menstrual and reproductive history, fibrocystic disease and epithelial hyperplasia, exogenous estrogens, contraceptive agents, and ionizing radiation. The vast majority of breast carcinomas are adenocarcinomas (ductal or lobular). Breast carcinoma spreads by direct invasion, by the lymphatic route, and by the blood vessel route. The most common site of lymph node involvement is the axilla." ;
    flat:display%20name "Breast Carcinoma" ;
    flat:parents "C9335|C2916" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Neoplastic Process" ;
    flat:synonyms "Breast Carcinoma|Breast Cancer|Breast Cancer|Breast Cancer|Breast Cancer|Breast Cancer|Breast Cancer|Breast cancer|Breast cancer, NOS|Carcinoma of Breast|Carcinoma of the Breast|Mammary Carcinoma|breast cancer" ;
.

