ncit:C49679
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C49679" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C49679>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SDTM Vital Sign Test Code Terminology|CDISC SDTM Vital Sign Test Name Terminology|CDISC SEND Cardiovascular Test Code Terminology|CDISC SEND Cardiovascular Test Name Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "The mean pressure of the blood within the arterial circulation. The arterial pressure may be directly measured by insertion of an intra-arterial catheter connected to a transducer. The mean arterial pressure (MAP) can be calculated by subsequent analysis of the waveform. MAP can be approximated without an invasive procedure using the following formula: diastolic pressure plus 1/3 of the pulse pressure, where pulse pressure is systolic pressure - diastolic pressure." ;
    flat:parents "C54706" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Quantitative Concept" ;
    flat:synonyms "Mean Arterial Pressure|MAP|MAP" ;
.

