    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM Evaluator Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology|FDA Individual Case Safety Report Terminology|Occupation ICSR Terminology|Operator of Medical Device ICSR Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "An individual trained and certified to apply knowledge of the concepts, principles, and practices of physical therapy for the treatment or prevention of physical disability or disease. Physical therapist plans and carries out treatment utilizing therapeutic exercise, massage, and physical agents such as air, water, electricity, sound, and radiant energy; performs tests and measurements involving manual or electrical means; and interpret results. Therapist also devises adaptations of equipment to meet the specific needs of patients." ;
    flat:parents "C28398" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Occupation or Discipline" ;
    flat:synonyms "Physical Therapist|PHYSICAL THERAPIST|PHYSIOTHERAPIST|Physiotherapist|physical therapist" ;
.

