ncit:C62234
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C62234" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C62234>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM ECG Finding Terminology|CDISC SDTM Holter ECG Results Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND ECG Standard Character Result Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "An electrocardiographic finding of a ventricular tachycardia in which the QRS complexes have a uniform morphology. (CDISC)" ;
    flat:parents "C111103" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Finding" ;
    flat:synonyms "Monomorphic Ventricular Tachycardia by ECG Finding|Monomorphic Ventricular Tachycardia|Monomorphic Ventricular Tachycardia by EKG Finding|VENTRICULAR TACHYCARDIA, MONOMORPHIC|Ventricular Tachycardia, Monomorphic|Ventricular tachycardia, monomorphic" ;
.

ncit:C62236
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C62236" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C62236>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM ECG Finding Terminology|CDISC SDTM Holter ECG Results Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND ECG Standard Character Result Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "An electrocardiographic finding of a ventricular tachycardia in which the QRS complexes have a variable morphology and often rate. (CDISC)" ;
    flat:parents "C111103" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Finding" ;
    flat:synonyms "Polymorphic Ventricular Tachycardia by ECG Finding|Polymorphic Ventricular Tachycardia|Polymorphic Ventricular Tachycardia by EKG Finding|VENTRICULAR TACHYCARDIA, POLYMORPHIC|Ventricular Tachycardia, Polymorphic|Ventricular tachycardia, polymorphic|Ventricular tachycardia, polymorphous" ;
.

ncit:C62239
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C62239" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C62239>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM ECG Finding Terminology|CDISC SDTM Holter ECG Results Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND ECG Standard Character Result Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "An electrocardiographic finding in which the sinus rate fluctuates with the respiratory cycle. (CDISC)" ;
    flat:parents "C80503" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Finding" ;
    flat:synonyms "Sinus Arrhythmia by ECG Finding|Respiratory Sinus Arrhythmia|SINUS ARRHYTHMIA|Sinus Arrhythmia|Sinus Arrhythmia by EKG Finding|Sinus arrhythmia" ;
.

ncit:C62240
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C62240" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C62240>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM ECG Finding Terminology|CDISC SDTM Holter ECG Results Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology|Neonatal Research Network Terminology|NICHD Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "An electrocardiographic finding of a supraventricular arrhythmia characterized by 3 or more distinct P wave morphologies with an isoelectric baseline, variable PR intervals and no predominant atrial rhythm. The ventricular rate is typically below 100 beats per minute. (CDISC)" ;
    flat:parents "C80503" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Finding" ;
    flat:synonyms "Wandering Atrial Pacemaker by ECG Finding|WANDERING ATRIAL PACEMAKER|Wandering Atrial Pacemaker|Wandering Atrial Pacemaker|Wandering Atrial Pacemaker by EKG Finding|Wandering atrial pacemaker" ;
.

ncit:C62242
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C62242" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C62242>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM ECG Finding Terminology|CDISC SDTM Holter ECG Results Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND ECG Standard Character Result Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "An electrocardiographic finding in which a failure of impulse formation or conduction in the sinus node produces prolongation of the P-P interval or dropped P waves. The threshold for the prolongation of the P-P interval is not well defined. (CDISC)" ;
    flat:parents "C27045" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Finding" ;
    flat:synonyms "Sinus Arrest by ECG Finding|SINUS ARREST/PAUSE|Sinus Arrest|Sinus Arrest by EKG Finding|Sinus Arrest/Pause|Sinus Pause|Sinus arrest/pause|Sinus pause or arrest" ;
.

ncit:C62243
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C62243" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C62243>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "Cellosaurus Disease Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "A derangement in the normal functioning of the sinoatrial node. Typically, SA node dysfunction is manifest as sinoatrial exit block or sinus arrest, but may present as an absolute or relative bradycardia in the presence of a stressor. It may be associated with bradycardia-tachycardia syndrome" ;
    flat:parents "C35552" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Finding" ;
    flat:synonyms "Sinus Node Dysfunction" ;
.

ncit:C62245
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C62245" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C62245>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM ECG Finding Terminology|CDISC SDTM Holter ECG Results Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND ECG Standard Character Result Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "An electrocardiographic finding of a regular atrial rhythm with atrial rate of less than 101 beats per minute which does not originate in the sinus node, and which is characterized by P waves whose morphology differs from the P wave morphology during sinus rhythm. (CDISC)" ;
    flat:parents "C80503" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Finding" ;
    flat:synonyms "Ectopic Atrial Rhythm by ECG Finding|ECTOPIC ATRIAL RHYTHM|Ectopic Atrial Rhythm|Ectopic Atrial Rhythm by EKG Finding|Ectopic Supraventricular Rhythm" ;
.

ncit:C62246
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C62246" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C62246>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM ECG Finding Terminology|CDISC SDTM Holter ECG Results Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND ECG Standard Character Result Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "An electrocardiographic finding of an abnormally short PR interval. Thresholds for different age, sex, and patient populations exist." ;
    flat:parents "C80503" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Finding" ;
    flat:synonyms "Short PR Interval by ECG Finding|SHORT PR INTERVAL|Short PR Interval|Short PR Interval by EKG Finding|Short PR interval" ;
.

ncit:C62248
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C62248" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C62248>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM ECG Finding Terminology|CDISC SDTM Holter ECG Results Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "An electrocardiographic finding of a type of atrioventricular dissociation characterized by the atria (P waves) and ventricles (QRS complexes) beating at similar rates, although independently. (CDISC)" ;
    flat:parents "C41328" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Finding" ;
    flat:synonyms "Isorhythmic Atrioventricular Dissociation|ISORHYTHMIC DISSOCIATION|Isorhythmic dissociation" ;
.

ncit:C62250
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C62250" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C62250>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM ECG Finding Terminology|CDISC SDTM Holter ECG Results Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND ECG Standard Character Result Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "An electrocardiographic finding of the sudden onset of transient AV block, which is often associated with preexisting conduction disorders. (CDISC)" ;
    flat:parents "C26703" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Finding" ;
    flat:synonyms "Paroxysmal Atrioventricular Block by ECG Finding|PAROXYSMAL AV BLOCK|Paroxysmal AV Block|Paroxysmal AV block|Paroxysmal Atrioventricular Block|Paroxysmal Atrioventricular Block by EKG Finding" ;
.

ncit:C62256
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C62256" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C62256>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM ECG Finding Terminology|CDISC SDTM Holter ECG Results Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND ECG Standard Character Result Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "An electrocardiographic finding of an ectopic impulse originating in the ventricles. The QRS morphology of these complexes is different from those of supraventricular origin. The QRS duration is often longer and the RR interval preceding the complexes is usually shorter than that of supraventricular beats. (CDISC)" ;
    flat:parents "C111101" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Finding" ;
    flat:synonyms "Ventricular Premature Complex by ECG Finding|PREMATURE VENTRICULAR COMPLEX|PVC|PVC|Premature Ventricular Complex|Premature Ventricular Complexes|VE|VES|VPC|VPC|Ventricular Extra Beat|Ventricular Premature Complex|Ventricular Premature Complex by EKG Finding|Ventricular Premature Complexes" ;
.

ncit:C62257
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C62257" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C62257>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM ECG Finding Terminology|CDISC SDTM Holter ECG Results Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND ECG Standard Character Result Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "An electrocardiographic finding of an ectopic impulse originating in the atria and not specifically in the sinus node. The P wave morphology of these complexes is often different from a sinus P wave and the RR intervals preceding these complexes is also shorter than those of the regular beats. (CDISC)" ;
    flat:parents "C80503" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Finding" ;
    flat:synonyms "Atrial Premature Complex by ECG Finding|APC|APC|Atrial Premature Complex|Atrial Premature Complex by EKG Finding|Atrial premature complex(es)|PAC|PAC|PREMATURE ATRIAL COMPLEXES|Premature Atrial Complex|Premature atrial complex|Premature atrial complexes|SVE|Supraventricular Extra Beat|Supraventricular Premature Beat" ;
.

ncit:C62258
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C62258" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C62258>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM ECG Finding Terminology|CDISC SDTM Holter ECG Results Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "An electrocardiographic finding of initial slurring (delta wave) of the QRS complex due to the presence of an accessory pathway. This characteristic ECG pattern is typically seen in Wolff-Parkinson-White syndrome. (CDISC)" ;
    flat:parents "C111075" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Finding" ;
    flat:synonyms "Delta Wave by ECG Finding|DELTA WAVE|Delta Wave|Delta Wave by EKG Finding|Delta wave" ;
.

ncit:C62259
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C62259" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C62259>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM ECG Finding Terminology|CDISC SDTM Holter ECG Results Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND ECG Standard Character Result Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "An electrocardiographic finding in which two premature ventricular complexes occur sequentially. (CDISC)" ;
    flat:parents "C111101" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Finding" ;
    flat:synonyms "Ventricular Couplet by ECG Finding|Couplet|VENTRICULAR COUPLET|Ventricular Couplet|Ventricular Couplet by EKG Finding|Ventricular Couplets|Ventricular Pair" ;
.

ncit:C62261
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C62261" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C62261>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM ECG Finding Terminology|CDISC SDTM Holter ECG Results Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND ECG Standard Character Result Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "An electrocardiographic finding of a regular supraventricular tachycardia which utilizes an atrioventricular bypass tract as its retrograde limb (orthodromic tachycardia) or as its antegrade limb (antidromic tachycardia). QRS complexes during sinus rhythm may show preexcitation. During orthodromic tachycardia the preexcitation is not present and a retrograde P wave may appear after the QRS complex. During antidromic tachycardia the QRS complex is preexcited. (CDISC)" ;
    flat:parents "C27045|C111100" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Finding" ;
    flat:synonyms "Atrioventricular Reentrant Tachycardia by ECG Finding|AV RE-ENTRANT TACHYCARDIA|AV Reentrant Supraventricular Tachycardia|AV Reentrant Tachycardia|Atrioventricular Reentrant Tachycardia|Atrioventricular Reentrant Tachycardia by EKG Finding" ;
.

ncit:C62266
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C62266" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C62266>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM ECG Finding Terminology|CDISC SDTM Holter ECG Results Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "An electrocardiographic finding of idioventricular rhythm with a rate greater than 50 beats per minute. (CDISC)" ;
    flat:parents "C111101" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Finding" ;
    flat:synonyms "Accelerated Idioventricular Rhythm by ECG Finding|ACCELERATED IDIOVENTRICULAR RHYTHM|AIVR|Accelerated Idioventricular Rhythm|Accelerated Idioventricular Rhythm by EKG Finding|Accelerated idioventricular rhythm" ;
.

ncit:C62267
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C62267" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C62267>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM ECG Finding Terminology|CDISC SDTM Holter ECG Results Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND ECG Standard Character Result Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "An electrocardiographic finding of a slightly widened QRS duration (typically less than 120 ms) with leftward frontal plane QRS axis and typically small Q waves in leads I and aVL. (CDISC)" ;
    flat:parents "C34665" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Finding" ;
    flat:synonyms "Left Anterior Fascicular Block by ECG Finding|LAFB|LEFT ANTERIOR FASCICULAR BLOCK|Left Anterior Fascicular Block|Left Anterior Fascicular Block by EKG Finding|Left Anterior Hemiblock|Left Anterior Hemiblock|Left anterior fascicular block" ;
.

ncit:C62268
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C62268" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C62268>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM ECG Finding Terminology|CDISC SDTM Holter ECG Results Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "An electrocardiographic finding of an S1Q3 pattern and QRS axis greater than or equal to 120 degrees. It is usually seen in association with other abnormalities (e.g. RBBB or RVH). (CDISC)" ;
    flat:parents "C34665" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Finding" ;
    flat:synonyms "Left Posterior Fascicular Block by ECG Finding|LEFT POSTERIOR FASCICULAR BLOCK|LPFB|Left Posterior Fascicular Block|Left Posterior Fascicular Block by EKG Finding|Left Posterior Hemiblock|Left Posterior Hemiblock|Left posterior fascicular block" ;
.

ncit:C62269
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C62269" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C62269>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "ACC/AHA Cardiovascular and Noncardiovascular Complications of COVID-19 Terminology|ACC/AHA COVID-19 Appendix Authorized Values|Appendix 7: Diagnostic Procedures Terminology|CDISC SDTM ECG Finding Terminology|CDISC SDTM Holter ECG Results Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND ECG Standard Character Result Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "An electrocardiographic finding of a wide QRS complex with evidence of delayed conduction to the left ventricle, manifested as a widened initial portion of the QRS complex in leads V5, V6, I and aVL and with QRS duration greater than or equal to 120 ms. (CDISC)" ;
    flat:parents "C84603" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Finding" ;
    flat:synonyms "Left Bundle Branch Block by ECG Finding|Complete LBBB|LBBB|LBBB|LEFT BUNDLE BRANCH BLOCK|Left Bundle Branch Block|Left Bundle Branch Block by EKG Finding|Left bundle branch block|Left bundle-branch block" ;
.

ncit:C62270
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C62270" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C62270>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "ACC/AHA Cardiovascular and Noncardiovascular Complications of COVID-19 Terminology|ACC/AHA COVID-19 Appendix Authorized Values|Appendix 7: Diagnostic Procedures Terminology|CDISC SDTM ECG Finding Terminology|CDISC SDTM Holter ECG Results Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND ECG Standard Character Result Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "An electrocardiographic finding of a wide QRS complex with evidence of delayed conduction to the right ventricle, manifested by a widened initial portion of the QRS in V1 and V2, a widened S wave in V5, V6, I and aVL, and with QRS duration greater than or equal to 120 ms.  An RsR' complex is typically present in leads V1 and V2. (CDISC)" ;
    flat:parents "C84603" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Finding" ;
    flat:synonyms "Right Bundle Branch Block by ECG Finding|Complete RBBB|RBBB|RBBB|RIGHT BUNDLE BRANCH BLOCK|Right Bundle Branch Block|Right Bundle Branch Block by EKG Finding|Right bundle branch block|Right bundle-branch block" ;
.

ncit:C62271
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C62271" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C62271>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "ACC/AHA Cardiovascular and Noncardiovascular Complications of COVID-19 Terminology|ACC/AHA COVID-19 Appendix Authorized Values|Appendix 7: Diagnostic Procedures Terminology|CDISC SDTM ECG Finding Terminology|CDISC SDTM Holter ECG Results Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND ECG Standard Character Result Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "An electrocardiographic finding of a widened QRS duration typically greater than 110 ms which does not meet the morphologic criteria for any of the standard bundle branch or fascicular block patterns. (CDISC)" ;
    flat:parents "C34665" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Finding" ;
    flat:synonyms "Nonspecific Intraventricular Conduction Delay by ECG Finding|INTRAVENTRICULAR CONDUCTION DELAY, NONSPECIFIC|IVCD|Intraventricular Conduction Defect|Intraventricular conduction delay|Nonspecific Intraventricular Conduction Delay|Nonspecific Intraventricular Conduction Delay by EKG Finding|Nonspecific intraventricular conduction delay" ;
.

