ncit:C62656
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C62656" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C62656>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM Laboratory Test Code Terminology|CDISC SDTM Laboratory Test Name Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology|GDC Terminology|GDC Value Terminology|OS Authorized Value Terminology|OS Lab Table" ;
    flat:definition "A measurement of the clotting time of plasma recalcified in the presence of excess tissue thromboplastin; it is a measure of the extrinsic pathway of coagulation. It is used to determine the clotting tendency of blood, in the measure of warfarin dosage, liver damage and vitamin K status. Factors measured are fibrinogen, prothrombin, and factors V, VII, and X." ;
