    flat:definition "The area between the x-axis and the curve given by the integrand. It is equal to the definite integral of a function. In the field of pharmacokinetics, the area under the curve (AUC) is the area under the curve in a plot of concentration of a drug in plasma against time. AUC is usually given for the time interval zero to infinity, and other time intervals are indicated." ;
    flat:parents "C25244" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Qualitative Concept" ;
    flat:synonyms "Area Under Curve|AUC|AUC|AUC|Area Under the Curve|{AUC}|{AUC}" ;
.

