ncit:C67264
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C67264" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C67264>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SDTM Unit of Measure Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology|FDA Structured Product Labeling Terminology|HL7 FHIR v5.0.0 R5 Unit of Measure Terminology|HL7 Unit of Measure Terminology|ICH Unit of Measure Terminology|SPL UCUM Terminology|UCUM Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "A measure of viable infectious entities (e.g. viral particles or group of particles) in the specimen or product defined as the smallest quantity that can produce a cytopathic effect in the host cell culture challenged with the defined inoculum, visible under the microscope and/or to the naked eye as a plaque. A number of plaque forming units (PFU) per unit volume is a conventional way to refer the titer of an infective entity in a specimen or preparation." ;
    flat:parents "C67373|C48470" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Quantitative Concept" ;
    flat:synonyms "Plaque Forming Unit|PFU|PFU|PFU|PLAQUE-FORMING UNITS|PLAQUE-FORMING UNITS|PLAQUE-FORMING UNITS|[PFU]|[PFU]|[PFU]|[PFU]|[PFU]|plaque forming unit|plaque forming units|{PFU}|{PFU}" ;
.

