    flat:definition "An electrocardiographic finding of a lack of progression of R wave height across precordial leads. (CDISC)" ;
    flat:parents "C90443" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Finding" ;
    flat:synonyms "Poor R Wave Progression by ECG Finding|POOR R WAVE PROGRESSION|Poor R Wave Progression|Poor R Wave Progression|Poor R Wave Progression by EKG Finding" ;
.

ncit:C71034
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C71034" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C71034>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM ECG Finding Terminology|CDISC SDTM Holter ECG Results Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND ECG Standard Character Result Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology|HL Authorized Value Terminology|HL Late Effects Table|NICHD Terminology|Pediatric Adverse Events Terminology Mapped to MedDRA|Pediatric Adverse Events Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "An electrocardiographic finding in which the QT interval not corrected for heart rate is prolonged. Thresholds for different age, sex, and patient populations exist." ;
    flat:parents "C111101" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Finding" ;
    flat:synonyms "Prolonged QT Interval by ECG Finding|PROLONGED QT|Prolonged QT|Prolonged QT|Prolonged QT|Prolonged QT Interval|Prolonged QT Interval by EKG Finding|Prolonged QT interval|QT Prolongation" ;
.

ncit:C71035
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C71035" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C71035>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM ECG Finding Terminology|CDISC SDTM Holter ECG Results Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "An electrocardiographic finding in which there is an alternating pattern of any of the waveform components." ;
    flat:parents "C111075" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Finding" ;
    flat:synonyms "Electrical Alternans by ECG Finding|ELECTRICAL ALTERNANS|Electrical Alternans|Electrical Alternans by EKG Finding|Electrical alternans" ;
.

ncit:C71039
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C71039" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C71039>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM ECG Finding Terminology|CDISC SDTM Holter ECG Results Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND ECG Standard Character Result Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "An electrocardiographic finding which comprises left, right or bilateral atrial enlargement. This is may be characterized by prolonged P wave duration, increased P wave amplitude, or multi-component P waves. (CDISC)" ;
    flat:parents "C41328" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Finding" ;
    flat:synonyms "Atrial Enlargement by ECG Finding|ATRIAL ENLARGEMENT|Atrial Enlargement|Atrial Enlargement by EKG Finding" ;
.

ncit:C71040
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C71040" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C71040>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM ECG Finding Terminology|CDISC SDTM Holter ECG Results Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "An electrocardiographic finding suggesting underlying hypertrophy or dilatation of the left atrium. Electrocardiographic criteria used for the diagnosis of left atrial abnormality may include a bifid p wave, a biphasic p wave and/or a p wave duration of greater than 0.12 seconds." ;
    flat:parents "C71039" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Finding" ;
    flat:synonyms "P-mitrale by ECG Finding|LEFT ATRIAL ABNORMALITY|Left Atrial Enlargement|Left Atrial Enlargement by ECG Finding|P-mitrale|P-mitrale|P-mitrale by EKG Finding" ;
.

ncit:C71041
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C71041" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C71041>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM ECG Finding Terminology|CDISC SDTM Holter ECG Results Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "An electrocardiographic finding suggesting underlying hypertrophy or dilatation of the right atrium. Electrocardiographic criteria used for the diagnosis of right atrial abnormality may include a peaked p wave greater than 2.5 millimeters in amplitude in the inferior leads." ;
    flat:parents "C71039" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Finding" ;
    flat:synonyms "P-pulmonale by ECG Finding|P-pulmonale|P-pulmonale|P-pulmonale by EKG Finding|RIGHT ATRIAL ABNORMALITY|Right Atrial Enlargement|Right Atrial Enlargement by ECG Finding" ;
.

ncit:C71042
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C71042" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C71042>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM ECG Finding Terminology|CDISC SDTM Holter ECG Results Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND ECG Standard Character Result Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "An electrocardiographic finding of three or more consecutive complexes of ventricular origin. The QRS complexes are wide and have an abnormal morphology. (CDISC)" ;
    flat:parents "C111101" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Finding" ;
    flat:synonyms "Ectopic Ventricular Rhythm by ECG Finding|ECTOPIC VENTRICULAR RHYTHM|Ectopic Ventricular Rhythm|Ectopic Ventricular Rhythm by EKG Finding|Ectopic ventricular rhythm" ;
.

ncit:C71044
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C71044" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C71044>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM ECG Finding Terminology|CDISC SDTM Holter ECG Results Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND ECG Standard Character Result Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "An electrocardiographic finding of a supraventricular rhythm where the ratio of impulses generated above the atrioventricular node to the number of impulses conducted through to the ventricles is 2:1. This is manifested on the ECG as 2 P waves per QRS complex. (CDISC)" ;
    flat:parents "C26703" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Finding" ;
    flat:synonyms "2:1 Atrioventricular Block by ECG Finding|2:1 AV BLOCK|2:1 AV block|2:1 Atrioventricular Block|2:1 Atrioventricular Block by EKG Finding" ;
.

ncit:C71045
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C71045" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C71045>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM ECG Finding Terminology|CDISC SDTM Holter ECG Results Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND ECG Standard Character Result Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "An electrocardiographic finding in which the electrical activity of the atria and ventricles are independent of one another. (CDISC)" ;
    flat:parents "C111075" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Finding" ;
    flat:synonyms "Atrioventricular Dissociation by ECG Finding|ATRIOVENTRICULAR DISSOCIATION|AV Dissociation|Atrioventricular Dissociation|Atrioventricular Dissociation by EKG Finding|Atrioventricular dissociation" ;
.

ncit:C71046
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C71046" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C71046>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM ECG Finding Terminology|CDISC SDTM Holter ECG Results Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "An electrocardiographic finding comprising right bundle branch block and left anterior fascicular block, or right bundle branch block and left posterior fascicular block. Defects occurring in two of the three divisions of the conduction system of the heart are considered bifascicular blocks. Technically left bundle branch block may be considered a bifascicular block." ;
    flat:parents "C34665" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Finding" ;
    flat:synonyms "Bifascicular Block by ECG Finding|BIFASCICULAR BLOCK|Bifascicular Block|Bifascicular Block by EKG Finding|Bifascicular block" ;
.

ncit:C71047
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C71047" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C71047>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM ECG Finding Terminology|CDISC SDTM Holter ECG Results Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND ECG Standard Character Result Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "An electrocardiographic finding of a wide QRS complex with evidence of delayed conduction to the left ventricle, manifest as a widened initial portion of the QRS complex in leads V5, V6, I and aVL and with QRS duration less than 120 ms. (CDISC)" ;
    flat:parents "C71049" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Finding" ;
    flat:synonyms "Incomplete Left Bundle Branch Block by ECG Finding|INCOMPLETE LEFT BUNDLE BRANCH BLOCK|Incomplete Left Bundle Branch Block|Incomplete Left Bundle Branch Block by EKG Finding|Incomplete left bundle branch block" ;
.

ncit:C71048
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C71048" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C71048>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM ECG Finding Terminology|CDISC SDTM Holter ECG Results Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND ECG Standard Character Result Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "An electrocardiographic finding of a wide QRS complex with evidence of delayed conduction to the right ventricle, manifested by a widened initial portion of the QRS in V1 and V2, a widened S wave in V5, V6, I and aVL, and with QRS duration less than 120 ms. (CDISC)" ;
    flat:parents "C71049" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Finding" ;
    flat:synonyms "Incomplete Right Bundle Branch Block by ECG Finding|INCOMPLETE RIGHT BUNDLE BRANCH BLOCK|Incomplete Right Bundle Branch Block|Incomplete Right Bundle Branch Block by EKG Finding|Incomplete right bundle branch block|Incomplete right bundle-branch block" ;
.

ncit:C71049
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C71049" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C71049>" ;
    flat:definition "An electrocardiographic finding of partially blocked cardiac electrical impulse conduction along the fibers of one or both bundle branches." ;
    flat:parents "C84603" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Finding" ;
    flat:synonyms "Incomplete Bundle Branch Block by ECG Finding|Incomplete Bundle Branch Block|Incomplete Bundle Branch Block by EKG Finding" ;
.

ncit:C71050
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C71050" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C71050>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM ECG Finding Terminology|CDISC SDTM Holter ECG Results Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND ECG Standard Character Result Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "An electrocardiographic finding of a supraventricular arrhythmia characterized by 3 or more distinct P wave morphologies with an isoelectric baseline, variable PR intervals and no predominant atrial rhythm. The ventricular rate is typically 100-150 beats per minute. (CDISC)" ;
    flat:parents "C80503" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Finding" ;
    flat:synonyms "Multifocal Atrial Tachycardia by ECG Finding|MULTIFOCAL ATRIAL TACHYCARDIA|Multifocal Atrial Tachycardia|Multifocal Atrial Tachycardia by EKG Finding|Multifocal atrial tachycardia" ;
.

ncit:C71051
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C71051" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C71051>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM ECG Finding Terminology|CDISC SDTM Holter ECG Results Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND ECG Standard Character Result Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "An electrocardiographic finding of a rhythm which originates in the AV junction and results in a normal heart rate. It is characterized by retrograde P waves which may be obscured by or may follow the QRS complexes. The QRS complexes may be narrow or may demonstrate aberration. (CDISC)" ;
    flat:parents "C80503" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Finding" ;
    flat:synonyms "Junctional Rhythm by ECG Finding|JUNCTIONAL RHYTHM|Junctional Rhythm|Junctional Rhythm by EKG Finding|Junctional rhythm" ;
.

ncit:C71052
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C71052" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C71052>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM ECG Finding Terminology|CDISC SDTM Holter ECG Results Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND ECG Standard Character Result Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "An electrocardiographic finding of ventricular tachycardia greater than 30 seconds in duration." ;
    flat:parents "C111103" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Finding" ;
    flat:synonyms "Sustained Ventricular Tachycardia by ECG Finding|SUSTAINED VENTRICULAR TACHYCARDIA|Sustained VT|Sustained Ventricular Tachycardia|Sustained Ventricular Tachycardia by EKG Finding|Sustained ventricular tachycardia|Ventricular Tachycardia, Sustained" ;
.

ncit:C71053
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C71053" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C71053>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM ECG Finding Terminology|CDISC SDTM Holter ECG Results Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "An electrocardiographic finding of ventricular tachycardia less than 30 seconds in duration." ;
    flat:parents "C111103" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Finding" ;
    flat:synonyms "Non-Sustained Ventricular Tachycardia by ECG Finding|NON-SUSTAINED VENTRICULAR TACHYCARDIA|Non-Sustained VT|Non-Sustained Ventricular Tachycardia|Non-Sustained Ventricular Tachycardia by EKG Finding|Non-sustained ventricular tachycardia|Ventricular Tachycardia, Non-Sustained|Ventricular tachycardia, unsustained" ;
.

ncit:C71054
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C71054" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C71054>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM ECG Finding Terminology|CDISC SDTM Holter ECG Results Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND ECG Standard Character Result Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "An electrocardiographic finding of a normal QRS followed by a premature ventricular contraction; a rhythmic pairing of normal and atypical beats originating in the ventricles in a 1-1 ratio." ;
    flat:parents "C111101" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Finding" ;
    flat:synonyms "Ventricular Bigeminy by ECG Finding|Bigeminy|VENTRICULAR BIGEMINY|Ventricular Bigeminy|Ventricular Bigeminy by EKG Finding" ;
.

ncit:C71055
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C71055" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C71055>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM ECG Finding Terminology|CDISC SDTM Holter ECG Results Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND ECG Standard Character Result Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "An electrocardiographic finding of two sinus beats followed by a premature ventricular complex for 3 or more consecutive cycles; a regularly irregular rhythm of normal and abnormal QRS complexes in a 2-1 ratio. (CDISC)" ;
    flat:parents "C111101" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Finding" ;
    flat:synonyms "Ventricular Trigeminy by ECG Finding|Trigeminy|VENTRICULAR TRIGEMINY|Ventricular Trigeminy|Ventricular Trigeminy by EKG Finding" ;
.

ncit:C71065
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C71065" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C71065>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM ECG Finding Terminology|CDISC SDTM Holter ECG Results Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "An electrocardiographic finding of pathologic Q waves with accompanying ST elevation in leads V3 and V4, which is suggestive of acute myocardial infarction of the anterior wall of the left ventricle. (CDISC)" ;
    flat:parents "C101596" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Finding" ;
    flat:synonyms "Acute Anterior Myocardial Infarction by ECG Finding|ACUTE ANTERIOR WALL MYOCARDIAL INFARCTION|Acute Anterior MI|Acute Anterior Myocardial Infarction by EKG Finding|Acute Anterior Wall Myocardial Infarction" ;
.

ncit:C71066
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C71066" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C71066>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM ECG Finding Terminology|CDISC SDTM Holter ECG Results Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "An electrocardiographic finding of pathologic Q waves with accompanying ST elevation in leads III, aVF and often II, which is suggestive of acute myocardial infarction of the inferior wall of the left ventricle. (CDISC)" ;
    flat:parents "C101596" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Finding" ;
    flat:synonyms "Acute Inferior Myocardial Infarction by ECG Finding|ACUTE INFERIOR WALL MYOCARDIAL INFARCTION|Acute Inferior MI|Acute Inferior Myocardial Infarction by EKG Finding|Acute Inferior Wall Myocardial Infarction" ;
.

ncit:C71067
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C71067" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C71067>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM ECG Finding Terminology|CDISC SDTM Holter ECG Results Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "An electrocardiographic finding of pathologic Q waves with accompanying ST elevation in leads V5, V6, I and aVL, which is suggestive of acute myocardial infarction of the lateral wall of the left ventricle. (CDISC)" ;
    flat:parents "C101596" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Finding" ;
    flat:synonyms "Acute Lateral Myocardial Infarction by ECG Finding|ACUTE LATERAL WALL MYOCARDIAL INFARCTION|Acute Lateral MI|Acute Lateral Myocardial Infarction by EKG Finding|Acute Lateral Wall Myocardial Infarction" ;
.

ncit:C71068
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C71068" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C71068>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM ECG Finding Terminology|CDISC SDTM Holter ECG Results Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "An electrocardiographic finding in leads V1 or V2 of an initial R wave duration greater than or equal to 40 ms, R wave greater than S wave, upright T wave, with accompanying ST elevation, which is suggestive of acute myocardial infarction of the posterior wall of the left ventricle. Evidence of inferior or lateral myocardial infarction is usually also present. (CDISC)" ;
    flat:parents "C101596" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Finding" ;
    flat:synonyms "Acute Posterior Myocardial Infarction by ECG Finding|ACUTE POSTERIOR WALL MYOCARDIAL INFARCTION|Acute Posterior MI|Acute Posterior Myocardial Infarction by EKG Finding|Acute Posterior Wall Myocardial Infarction" ;
.

ncit:C71069
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C71069" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C71069>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM ECG Finding Terminology|CDISC SDTM Holter ECG Results Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "An electrocardiographic finding of pathologic Q waves in leads V3 and V4, which is suggestive of myocardial infarction of the anterior wall of the left ventricle. (CDISC)" ;
    flat:parents "C101589" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Finding" ;
    flat:synonyms "Anterior Myocardial Infarction by ECG Finding|ANTERIOR WALL MYOCARDIAL INFARCTION|Anterior MI|Anterior Myocardial Infarction by EKG Finding|Anterior Wall Myocardial Infarction" ;
.

ncit:C71073
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C71073" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C71073>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM ECG Finding Terminology|CDISC SDTM Holter ECG Results Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND ECG Standard Character Result Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "An electrocardiographic finding of a delay in impulse propagation through the atria. This is characterized by broad P waves which are often biphasic in V1. (CDISC)" ;
    flat:parents "C80503" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Finding" ;
    flat:synonyms "Intra-Atrial Conduction Delay by ECG Finding|INTRAATRIAL CONDUCTION DELAY|Intra-Atrial Conduction Delay|Intra-Atrial Conduction Delay by EKG Finding|Intraatrial Conduction Delay" ;
.

ncit:C71074
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
