    flat:definition "An electrocardiographic finding of three or more consecutive wide QRS complexes of uncertain origin with a rate greater than a certain threshold (100 or 120 beats per minute are commonly used). (CDISC)" ;
    flat:parents "C111103" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Finding" ;
    flat:synonyms "Wide QRS Tachycardia by ECG Finding|WIDE QRS TACHYCARDIA|Wide QRS Tachycardia|Wide QRS Tachycardia by EKG Finding|Wide QRS tachycardia|Wide-QRS tachycardia" ;
.

ncit:C71091
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C71091" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C71091>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM Microorganism Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology|CTRP Biomarker Terminology|CTRP Terminology|FDA Established Names and Unique Ingredient Identifier Codes Terminology|NICHD Terminology|Pediatric Immunization Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "An icosahedral, enveloped virus containing a single molecule of linear double-stranded DNA of 125000 nucleotides that infects only humans. It is the causative agent of chickenpox and shingles." ;
    flat:display%20name "Varicella Zoster Virus" ;
    flat:parents "C112426" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Virus" ;
    flat:synonyms "Varicella Zoster Virus|HHV-3|HHV-3|HHV3|HUMAN HERPESVIRUS 3|Herpes Zoster Virus|Human Alphaherpesvirus 3|Human Herpesvirus 3|Human Herpesvirus 3|VARICELLA ZOSTER VIRUS|VZV|VZV|Varicella-Zoster Virus 1" ;
.

ncit:C71092
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C71092" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C71092>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM ECG Test Method Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "This is a measurement of electric heart vectors whereby this type of measurement aims to create an orthonormal measurement of the electric cardiac vector." ;
    flat:parents "C62085" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Quantitative Concept" ;
    flat:synonyms "Vectorcardiograph Corrected|VECTORCARDIOGRAPH CORRECTED" ;
.

ncit:C71093
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C71093" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C71093>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM ECG Test Method Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "A measurement of electric heart vectors whereby this type of measurement does not consider the distortions caused by the boundary and internal inhomogeneities of the body. These lead systems assure the direction of the spatial line connecting an electrode pair and yields the orientation of the corresponding lead vectors." ;
    flat:parents "C62085" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Quantitative Concept" ;
    flat:synonyms "Vectorcardiograph Uncorrected|VECTORCARDIOGRAPH UNCORRECTED" ;
.

ncit:C71094
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C71094" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C71094>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM ECG Finding Terminology|CDISC SDTM Holter ECG Results Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "An electrocardiographic finding of the Q axis from -30 to -90 degrees." ;
    flat:parents "C41355" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Finding" ;
    flat:synonyms "Q Axis Left Axis Deviation|Left-axis deviation|Q AXIS, LEFT AXIS DEVIATION|Q Axis, Left axis deviation|QRS axis, left axis deviation" ;
.

ncit:C71095
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C71095" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C71095>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM ECG Finding Terminology|CDISC SDTM Holter ECG Results Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "An electrocardiographic finding of the Q axis from +90 to +180 degrees." ;
    flat:parents "C41355" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Finding" ;
    flat:synonyms "Q Axis Right Axis Deviation|Q AXIS, RIGHT AXIS DEVIATION|Q Axis, Right axis deviation|QRS axis, right axis deviation|Right-axis deviation" ;
.

ncit:C71100
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C71100" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C71100>" ;
    flat:definition "The spatial property of the way in which an electrocardiogram lead is placed on the body." ;
    flat:parents "C45788" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Spatial Concept" ;
    flat:synonyms "Lead Placement" ;
.

ncit:C71101
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C71101" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C71101>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM ECG Test Method Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND ECG Method Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "An electrocardiogram (ECG) lead placement whereby 12 leadpoints are recorded but the position of the leads is unspecified." ;
    flat:parents "C71100" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Classification" ;
    flat:synonyms "12 Lead Placement Unspecified|12 LEAD UNSPECIFIED|12 Lead Unspecified" ;
.

ncit:C71102
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C71102" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C71102>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM ECG Test Method Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND ECG Method Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "An electrocardiogram (ECG) lead placement whereby 12 leads are recorded, with each lead representing an electrical \"view\" of the heart. The six leads recorded in the frontal plane are derived from the placement of 3 electrodes (RA or Right Arm, LA, or Left Arm, and LL or Left Leg). These bipolar frontal leads form the basis of Einthoven's triangle, and are represented by leads I, II, and III.  Three other derived (or augmented) bipolar frontal vectors are also recorded on a standard 12-lead EKG, aVR, aVF, and aVL. 6 unipolar leads, corresponding to V1 - V6 measure the electrical activity in the horizontal plane. The placement for the \"V\" leads is as follows: V1: right 4th intercostal space,V2: left 4th intercostal space, V3: halfway between V2 and V4, V4: left 5th intercostal space, mid-clavicular line, V5: horizontal to V4, anterior axillary line, V6: horizontal to V5, mid-axillary line." ;
    flat:parents "C71100" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Classification" ;
    flat:synonyms "12 Lead Placement Standard|12 LEAD STANDARD|12 Lead Standard" ;
.

ncit:C71103
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C71103" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C71103>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM ECG Test Method Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "An electrocardiogram (ECG) lead placement whereby 12 leadpoints are recorded but the standard lead positions have been modified for ECG recording during exercise. Exercise stress testing requires moving the limb electrodes to more central positions on the thorax. The electrodes are placed in bony prominences close to the bases of the respective limbs in order to avoid skeletal muscle artifact, provide stability for recording electrodes and to record waveforms similar to the standard limb sites." ;
    flat:parents "C71100" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Classification" ;
    flat:synonyms "12 Lead Placement Mason Likar|12 LEAD MASON LIKAR|12 Lead Mason Likar" ;
.

ncit:C71104
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C71104" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C71104>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC Glossary Terminology|CDISC MRCT Center Clinical Research Glossary|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology|CTDC Node Terminology|CTRP Intervention Terminology|CTRP Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "A research study that prospectively assigns human participants or groups of humans to one or more health-related interventions to evaluate the effects on health outcomes." ;
    flat:display%20name "Clinical Trial" ;
    flat:parents "C208216" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Research Activity" ;
    flat:synonyms "Clinical Trial|Clinical Trials|Clinical Trials, Unspecified|Interventional Clinical Trial|Interventional Study|Trial|Trials|clinical trial|clinical trial|clinical trial|clinical trial|clinical_trial" ;
.

ncit:C71110
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C71110" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C71110>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM ECG Test Method Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "An electrocardiogram (ECG) lead placement whereby 12 leadpoints are recorded but the Mason Likar lead positions have been modified so that V1 to V6 on the chest are part of a single electrode pad. In addition, lead CM5 is substituted for lead aVR." ;
    flat:parents "C71100" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Classification" ;
    flat:synonyms "12 Lead Placement Mason Likar Modified|12 LEAD MODIFIED MASON LIKAR|12 Lead Modified Mason Likar" ;
.

ncit:C71112
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C71112" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C71112>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM ECG Test Method Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "An electrocardiogram (ECG) lead placement whereby 12 leadpoints are recorded but the standard lead positions have been modified so that all leads on the chest are part of a single electrode pad." ;
    flat:parents "C71100" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Classification" ;
    flat:synonyms "12 Lead Placement Chest|12 LEAD SINGLE PAD|12 Lead Single Pad" ;
.

ncit:C71113
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C71113" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C71113>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "The terminology subset that includes terms pertaining to frequency scheduling of interventions and medications within the Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium (CDISC) Study Data Tabulation Model (SDTM)." ;
    flat:parents "C77526|C66830" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Intellectual Product" ;
    flat:synonyms "CDISC SDTM Frequency Terminology|FREQ|Frequency|SDTM-FREQ" ;
.

ncit:C71114
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C71114" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C71114>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM ECG Test Method Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "An electrocardiogram (ECG) lead placement whereby the limb leads are placed on the torso for easier and faster application in emergency situations." ;
    flat:parents "C71100" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Classification" ;
    flat:synonyms "12 Lead Placement Non-Standard|12 LEAD NON-STANDARD|12 Lead Non-Standard" ;
.

ncit:C71115
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C71115" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C71115>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM ECG Test Method Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "Limb leads on the back (shoulder and on the hips)." ;
    flat:parents "C71100" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Classification" ;
    flat:synonyms "Lead Placement Bicycle|STANDARD LEADS FOR BICYCLE EXERCISE" ;
.

ncit:C71116
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C71116" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C71116>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM ECG Test Method Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "An electrocardiogram (ECG) lead placement whereby the display of the 12 standard ECG leads is in an 'orderly' sequence in a single horizontal display of: aVL, I, -aVR, II, aVF, III, V1 to V6. In the Cabrera display the limb lead aVR is inverted (-aVR) to obtain the same positive leftward orientation as the other 5 limbs." ;
    flat:parents "C71100" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Classification" ;
    flat:synonyms "12 Lead Placement Cabrera|12 LEAD CABRERA|12 Lead Cabrera" ;
.

ncit:C71117
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C71117" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C71117>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM ECG Test Method Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "An electrocardiographic lead placement schema in which the \"V\" leads are placed one intercostal space cephalad to the position they would have in the standard lead placement schema." ;
    flat:parents "C71100" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Classification" ;
    flat:synonyms "Lead Placement Standard Intercostal Space Higher|STANDARD LEADS ONE INTERCOSTAL SPACE HIGHER|Standard leads one intercostal space higher" ;
.

ncit:C71118
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C71118" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C71118>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM ECG Test Method Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "An electrocardiogram (ECG) lead placement for determining 3 orthogonal components X (right to left direction), Y (foot to head direction) and Z (back to front direction) of the heart. For this method a minimum of 4 electrodes are needed that represent the right arm, left arm, left leg and back. However, ususally 7 electrodes are used to avoid dependence on the dipole location and facilitate interpretation." ;
    flat:parents "C71100" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Classification" ;
    flat:synonyms "Lead Placement Frank|FRANK LEAD SYSTEM|Frank lead system" ;
.

ncit:C71119
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C71119" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C71119>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM ECG Test Method Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "An electrocardiogram (ECG) lead placement for determining 3 orthogonal components X (back to front), Y (right to left) and Z (foot to head) of the heart. This system places the electrodes closer to the heart to achieve better orthogonality and a homogeneous lead field." ;
    flat:parents "C71100" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Classification" ;
    flat:synonyms "Lead Placement McFee-Parungao|MCFEE-PARUNGAO LEAD SYSTEM|McFee-Parungao lead system" ;
.

ncit:C71120
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C71120" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C71120>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM ECG Test Method Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "An electrocardiogram (ECG) lead placement that is a type of uncorrected vectorcardiograph. This lead system is based on a rectangular body axis. It uses an extra number of electrodes to make it three-dimensional." ;
    flat:parents "C71100" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Classification" ;
    flat:synonyms "Lead Placement Cube|CUBE LEAD SYSTEM|Cube lead system" ;
.

ncit:C71121
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C71121" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C71121>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM ECG Test Method Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "An electrocardiogram (ECG) lead placement whereby the X+ lead is placed at the right mid-axillary line at the 4th intercostal space, X- at the left mid-axillary line at the 4th intercostal space, Y+ at the proximal left leg, Y- at the superior aspect of the manubrium, Z+ at the direct posterior to Z- and Z- at the 4th intercostal space at the left sternal margin." ;
    flat:parents "C71100" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Classification" ;
    flat:synonyms "Lead Placement Bipolar Uncorrected XYZ|BIPOLAR UNCORRECTED XYZ LEAD SYSTEM|Bipolar uncorrected XYZ lead system" ;
.

ncit:C71122
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C71122" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C71122>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM ECG Test Method Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "An electrocardiogram (ECG) lead placement that allows monitoring and recording of cardiac electrical activity. A V1-type lead is used whose positive electrode is localized in the 4th intercostal space, 2.5cm from the sternum. Its negative electrode is placed below the left clavicle. An addition of lead V5 and aVF can be made to facilitate interpretation." ;
    flat:parents "C71100" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Classification" ;
    flat:synonyms "Lead Placement Pseudo Orthogonal XYZ|PSEUDO-ORTHOGONAL XYZ LEAD SYSTEM|Pseudo-orthogonal XYZ lead system" ;
.

ncit:C71123
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C71123" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C71123>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM ECG Test Method Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "An electrocardiogram (ECG) lead placement whereby 4 chest electrodes and 1 reference electrode are used to allow for continuous monitoring at the clinical level. This placement creates a 12 lead ECG that allows the acquisition of simultaneous events in the frontal, horizontral and sagittal heart planes with the linear transformation of vectors. This system provides a three-dimensional portrayal of the heart and uses mathematical and fixed coefficients for each lead." ;
    flat:parents "C71100" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Classification" ;
    flat:synonyms "Lead Placement EASI Dower Transformation|12 LEAD EASI DOWER TRANSFORMATION|12 Lead EASI Dower Transformation" ;
.

ncit:C71124
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C71124" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C71124>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM Frequency Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "Every five days." ;
    flat:parents "C64493" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Temporal Concept" ;
    flat:synonyms "Every Five Days|Every 5 days|Q5D" ;
.

ncit:C71125
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C71125" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C71125>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM ECG Test Method Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "An electrocardiogram (ECG) lead placement whereby 12 leadpoints are recorded but one standard lead position is missing therefore requiring a Mortara source consistency filter." ;
    flat:parents "C71100" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Classification" ;
    flat:synonyms "12 Lead Placement 1 Lead Missing|12 LEAD 1 LEAD MISSING|12 Lead 1 Lead Missing" ;
.

ncit:C71126
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C71126" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C71126>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM ECG Test Method Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "An electrocardiogram (ECG) lead placement whereby 12 leadpoints are recorded but the standard lead positions have been modified so that the bipolar lead groups place the negative of the reference electrode over the manubrium (CM5), the right scapula (CB5), V5R (CC5) or on the forehead (CH5) and the active electrode at V5." ;
    flat:parents "C71100" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Classification" ;
    flat:synonyms "12 Lead Placement Standard And CC5-CM5-CH5|STANDARD 12-LEAD AND CM5-CC5-CH5|Standard 12-lead and CM5-CC5-CH5" ;
.

ncit:C71127
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C71127" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C71127>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM Frequency Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology|Operational Ontology for Radiation Oncology Prostate Cancer Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "Every two weeks." ;
    flat:parents "C64493" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Temporal Concept" ;
    flat:synonyms "Every Two Weeks|EVERY 2 WEEKS|Every 2 weeks|Every other week|Q2S" ;
.

ncit:C71128
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C71128" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C71128>" ;
    flat:concept%20in%20subset "CDISC SDTM ECG Test Method Terminology|CDISC SDTM Terminology|CDISC SEND Terminology|Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium Terminology" ;
    flat:definition "An electrocardiogram (ECG) lead placement whereby 12 leadpoints are recorded but the standard lead positions have been modified so that the negative reference is at CM5 and the active electrode is at the left leg position." ;
    flat:parents "C71100" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Classification" ;
    flat:synonyms "12 Lead Placement Standard And CC5-CM5-ML|STANDARD 12-LEAD AND CC5-CM5-ML|Standard 12-lead and CC5-CM5-ML" ;
.

ncit:C71129
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/ncit-flat#Thesaurus> ;
    flat:code "C71129" ;
    flat:concept%20IRI "<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C71129>" ;
