    flat:definition "Studies in which individuals are assigned by an investigator based on a protocol to receive specific interventions. Subjects may receive diagnostic, therapeutic or other types of interventions. The assignment of the intervention may or may not be random. The individuals are then followed and biomedical and/or health outcomes are assessed." ;
    flat:parents "C71104" ;
    flat:semantic%20type "Research Activity" ;
    flat:synonyms "Interventional Study|INTERVENTIONAL|Interventional Trial" ;
.

